.\" webdp8(1) manual page
.TH WEBDP8 1 "December 2025" "waffle8" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
webdp8 \- HTTP front\-end for the PDP\-8 emulator
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 tools/webdp8.py
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B webdp8
is a lightweight Flask server that wraps the PDP\-8 emulator shared library
(.B factory/libpdp8.so )
with a JSON REST API and minimal HTML control room. It creates the host
simulator board so the TC08 DECtape controller (device 076/077), KL8E console,
and line printer are attached on startup. Console and printer output are written
to temporary files that the API exposes.
.
The server listens on
.B 0.0.0.0:5000
when run directly; there are no command\-line flags. Build the shared library
before launching:
.IP
.EX
cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -fPIC -shared src/emulator/*.c -o factory/libpdp8.so
python3 tools/webdp8.py
.EE
.
.SH ENDPOINTS
All numeric values are octal strings unless noted.
.TP
.B GET /regs
Return PC, AC, LINK, switch register, HALT state, and cycle counter.
.TP
.B GET /mem?addr=<octal>&len=<n>
Read
.I len
words starting at
.IR addr .
.TP
.B PUT /mem
Write one word ({addr,val}) or a block ({start,values}).
.TP
.B POST /loader
Upload a Motorola S\-record (S1/S9) and load it into memory; sets PC if the
record supplies a start address and clears HALT.
.TP
.B POST /api/pdp8/assemble
Assemble source and return SREC (optionally a listing).
.TP
.B POST /api/pdp8/assemble_and_load
Assemble, load into memory, set PC (respecting start override), and clear HALT.
.TP
.B GET /trace?start=<pc>&cycles=<n>
Step up to
.I n
cycles (max 1024), returning per\-step register traces.
.TP
.B GET /output/teleprinter
Return KL8E console output since last read; ?peek=1 leaves the read pointer.
.TP
.B POST /input/keyboard
Queue ASCII into the KL8E keyboard buffer ({chars:string}).
.TP
.B GET /output/printer
Return line\-printer output since last read.
.TP
.B GET|PUT /switch
Read or set the PDP\-8 switch register (OSR/SKP chains).
.TP
.B GET /tc08/status
Report TC08 unit metadata (path, layout, size, writability, existence).
.TP
.B GET /tc08/dir/<unit>
Parse OS/8 directory segments from the unit image; returns segment headers and
entries with block numbers (octal and decimal).
.TP
.B GET /tc08/block/<unit>/<block>
Read a DECtape block. Defaults to OS/8 logical layout; override with
.BR ?layout=physical .
Add
.BR ?sixbit=1
to include sixbit rendering of each word.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TC08_IMAGE0
Path to the read-only DECtape image for TC08 unit 0
(default
.BR media/tape0.tu56 ).
.TP
.B TC08_IMAGE1
Path to the read/write DECtape image for TC08 unit 1
(default
.BR media/tape1.tu56 ).
.TP
.B FLASK_APP , FLASK_ENV
Ignored when invoking
.BR webdp8
directly; the script runs Flask internally on port 5000.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B tools/webdp8.py
Server implementation.
.TP
.B factory/libpdp8.so
Native emulator shared library loaded by the server.
.TP
.B templates/index.html
Minimal web UI served at
.BR / .
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Load a program and trace 16 steps:
.EX
curl -F \"file=@demo/cal3.srec\" http://127.0.0.1:5000/loader
curl \"http://127.0.0.1:5000/trace?cycles=16\"
.EE
.TP
Mount alternative DECtapes before launch:
.EX
export TC08_IMAGE0=tapes/os8.tu56
export TC08_IMAGE1=/tmp/scratch.tu56
python3 tools/webdp8.py
.EE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdp8 (1),
.BR tc08 (1),
.BR blkvue (1)
.
